      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# 3 · Define Persona, Debate, and Strategy\n## 5:32–18:19\n\nLionel analyzes Andy Wilson's self-presentation as a master debater, distinguishes debate from discussion or confrontation, and argues that Candace has been transformed from commentator into subject. He says a serious response should address evidence and reasonable doubt rather than her character. \n\nHe then interprets debate offers as possible attempts to redirect Candace's attention and explains why declining them may be strategically rational. \n\n**Function:** construct the standards and motive model that will be applied to the clips.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786055142666,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
