        "markdown": "# 5 · Diagnose Deflection and Reconstruct Answer\n## 25:16–35:16\n\nAs the source compares Charlie Kirk with other figures and discusses outside ideological influence, Lionel repeatedly says the answer is changing the subject. He then supplies a counterfactual response that, in his view, would have handled uncertainty more competently: acknowledge the possibility, distinguish motive from proof, and return to available evidence. \n\nWhen the source offers a left-wing-conspiracy alternative, Lionel interprets it as controlling the narrative by repeating another narrative. \n\n**Function:** classify an argumentative tactic and demonstrate the answer Lionel believes should have been given.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786055142666,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
