        "markdown": "# 8 · Epistemic Frame and Lay Incredulity\n## 52:16–1:01:49\n\nLionel separates several rings of the controversy: who committed the act, what can be proved at trial, TPUSA and Erica Kirk, and Candace Owens. He stresses that observers are not parties to the case and may not possess decisive information. \n\nHe then argues that a layperson's inability to imagine a mechanism does not disprove it, using ballistics, 9/11, covert weapons, and a historical umbrella assassination as analogies. \n\n**Function:** define what ignorance does and does not justify while broadening the media critique into a theory of public reasoning.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786055142666,
