        "markdown": "# 9 · Limited Hangout and Platform Incentives\n## 1:01:49–1:09:38\n\nLionel argues that the appearance may have introduced a large audience to claims they had never heard. He explains his concept of a limited hangout as revealing a small, manageable piece of a larger story so the public believes the subject has been exhausted. \n\nHe then speculates about the incentives that can make prominent figures avoid pushing dangerous or career-threatening subjects too far. \n\n**Function:** move from the argument's content to the media system and incentives surrounding its presentation.",
