        "markdown": "# 10 · Autobiographical Legitimation\n## 1:09:38–1:16:46\n\nLionel asks what question still confounds the audience, then recounts living in New York during and after 9/11. He describes his own movement from expecting universal curiosity to discovering that many people resist questions about painful public events. \n\nHe connects that experience back to the current case and argues that people demand more rigorous inquiry when someone they personally love is affected. \n\n**Function:** establish personal authority and explain the emotional origin of Lionel's inquiry-centered worldview.",
