          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧬 Observed Grammar\n\n**reversal thesis -> sponsor break -> define opponent persona -> define valid standard -> frame strategic motive -> select source exhibit -> pause immediately -> diagnose tactic -> replay statement -> reconstruct better answer -> audit omitted evidence -> select second exhibit -> correct the source's formulation -> broaden into epistemology and media incentives -> autobiographical legitimation -> jury recap -> reflective audience close**\n\nThis is a hybrid composition:\n\n- the **thesis** determines what the episode is trying to prove\n- the **source excerpts** function as exhibits\n- the **forensic audit** supplies supporting material\n- the **jury reenactment** provides the final proof test\n\nThe source timeline does not govern the full episode.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786055142666,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study04-replay",
      "type": "markdown",
