        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🔁 New Discovery · Replay and Repair\n\nStudy 03 established `play -> pause -> comment -> resume`.\n\nStudy 04 adds two important operations:\n\n## Replay\nLionel asks to hear a statement again and reuses the same source passage as the object of a second inspection.\n\n## Counterfactual repair\nHe does not only criticize the answer. He performs the answer he believes a competent or honest respondent should have given.\n\nA reusable media-commentary node may therefore need:\n\n- source range\n- commentary range\n- playback action: play, pause, resume, or replay\n- criticized argumentative move\n- standard being applied\n- reconstructed answer\n- relationship to earlier commentary\n\nThis is richer than a simple timestamped annotation.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786055142666,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
