      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🎙️ Commentary Roles Observed\n\nStudy 04 expands the possible `commentaryRole` vocabulary:\n\n- **identifies hesitation**\n- **diagnoses deflection**\n- **tests relevance**\n- **disputes a factual premise**\n- **distinguishes evidence from proof**\n- **distinguishes hypothesis from accusation**\n- **corrects a technical formulation**\n- **replays for emphasis**\n- **reconstructs a stronger answer**\n- **returns to omitted evidence**\n- **infers strategic motive**\n- **evaluates the opponent's persona**\n- **connects the exchange to platform incentives**\n\nOne broad `Lionel Comments on Media` class may still work, but this episode argues for structured role, target, and evaluative-standard fields.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
