      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🎛️ Container and Production Grammar\n\nThis specimen adds show-level elements that are not rhetorical claims:\n\n- **Sponsor Break** after the hook\n- **Live Chat Acknowledgment** during the analysis\n- **Super Chat Thanks** near the close\n- **Possible Later Stream Announcement**\n- **Subscription, like, and notification ritual**\n\nThese should belong to the episode container or publishing layer rather than the Lionel argument ontology.\n\nThe sponsor break is especially structural because it separates the promotional hook from the long analytical body. A template should preserve that insertion point without treating the advertisement as evidence or commentary.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
