          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧪 Provisional Node Types\n\n## Lionel-oriented candidates\n1. **Lionel Frames an Opponent**\n2. **Lionel Defines an Evaluative Standard**\n3. **Lionel Audits an Argument**\n4. **Lionel Diagnoses Deflection**\n5. **Lionel Replays Media**\n6. **Lionel Reconstructs an Answer**\n7. **Lionel Returns to Omitted Evidence**\n8. **Lionel Separates Analytical Questions**\n9. **Lionel Performs a Juror Test**\n10. **Lionel Adds Autobiographical Context**\n11. **Lionel Reflects with the Audience**\n\n## Shared production candidates\n12. **Sponsor Break**\n13. **Live Audience Acknowledgment**\n14. **Programming Announcement**\n\n## Possible consolidation\n`Lionel Audits an Argument`, `Lionel Diagnoses Deflection`, and `Lionel Reconstructs an Answer` may be roles or child structures of a broader **Lionel Comments on Media** class rather than three permanent classes.",
        "memo": "",
