      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🔬 Comparison Across Four Studies\n\n## Study 01 · Thesis Monologue\n**Spine:** one proposition developed through case, context, synthesis, and audience direction.\n\n## Study 02 · Hosted Forensic Commentary\n**Spine:** serial evidence anomalies inside another host's container.\n\n## Study 03 · Annotated Media Reaction\n**Spine:** the source clip's timeline. Lionel repeatedly pauses and interprets it.\n\n## Study 04 · Thesis-Led Adversarial Media Audit\n**Spine:** Lionel's claim that an opponent's media appearance failed. Selected source passages are exhibits used to prove that claim.\n\n## Critical distinction\nStudy 03 asks:\n**What does this source mean?**\n\nStudy 04 asks:\n**Why did this source argument fail, and what should it have done instead?**\n\nBoth use `Lionel Comments on Media`, but the surrounding grammar and purpose differ.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
