      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# ⚖️ Required Claim and Evidence Separation\n\nThis episode contains rapid movement among several epistemic categories:\n\n- words actually played from the source\n- Lionel's paraphrase of the source\n- Lionel's criticism of the source\n- allegations about motives or payment\n- descriptions of reported evidence\n- hypotheses about responsibility\n- legal arguments about reasonable doubt\n- autobiographical analogy\n- our structural observations\n\nA production graph should never flatten these into one undifferentiated narrative.\n\nUseful fields or relationships include:\n\n- `speaker`\n- `claimKind`\n- `assertedBy`\n- `sourceRange`\n- `evidenceReferenced`\n- `certainty`\n- `supports`\n- `contradicts`\n- `reframes`\n- `speculatesAbout`\n- `structuralObservation`\n\nThis separation protects both provenance and interpretability.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786055142666,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study04-model",
      "type": "markdown",
