      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-argument-audit-study-04"
        },
        "markdown": "# 📏 Confidence and Next Test\n\n## High confidence\n- source media may function as an exhibit without controlling the episode timeline\n- replay must be supported as a first-class playback transition\n- reconstructed answers are analytically different from ordinary commentary\n- sponsor and live-audience elements belong outside the argument ontology\n- Study 04 is compositionally distinct from Study 03\n\n## Medium confidence\n- `Lionel Audits an Argument` deserves a dedicated class\n- `Lionel Reconstructs an Answer` deserves a dedicated class rather than a role property\n- autobiography is a recurring Lionel move rather than a one-off expansion\n\n## Next useful specimen\nA shorter argument-reaction episode could reveal whether this structure is inherently long-form or whether the same grammar survives in a compact version.\n\nA second adversarial audit should also test whether replay, counterfactual repair, and sponsor placement recur.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786055142666,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    }
